With the CUSMA six-year review now formally underway, I wanted to flag two specific planning items it connects to for you.<br><br>
First, account placement for US holdings. If you hold US-listed dividend payers or US equity ETFs, the account they sit in matters for tax purposes. US dividends paid into an RRSP are exempt from the 15% US withholding tax under the Canada-US treaty. The same exemption does not apply to TFSAs. I want to confirm your current structure is optimized for this.<br><br>
Second, foreign property reporting. The CAD has weakened approximately 4.5% against the US dollar over the past year. If you hold US securities in non-registered accounts, the Canadian dollar value of those holdings may have increased without any new purchases. The T1135 foreign property form is required if that value exceeds $100,000 CAD at any point in the year. I would like to review your position before year-end.<br><br>
I will reach out next week to go through both items. No action is needed from you before then.<br><br>
[Your Name]<br><br>
<em>This communication is for educational purposes only and does not constitute personalized investment advice.</em>
</div>
