First, if you hold US dividend-paying securities in a TFSA, you are likely paying a 15% US withholding tax on those dividends that would not apply inside an RRSP. The Canada-US tax treaty protects RRSP accounts but not TFSAs. The annual cost on a reasonable-sized position is several hundred to several thousand dollars per year.<br><br>
Second, the Canadian dollar has weakened approximately 4.5% against the US dollar over the past year. If you hold US securities in non-registered accounts, the CAD value of those holdings has increased without any new purchases. The T1135 foreign property reporting form is required if that value exceeds $100,000 CAD. The penalty for missing the filing is automatic.<br><br>
If either of these is relevant to your situation and worth a conversation, I am happy to connect this week.<br><br>
[Your Name]<br><br>
