US and Iranian technical teams met indirectly in Doha on Tuesday and Wednesday, with Qatar mediating. Qatar confirmed "positive progress" on the June 17 ceasefire agreement''''s implementation, particularly around shipping administration and the release of frozen Iranian funds. The next round of talks will begin after the Khamenei funeral ends July 9.<br><br>
Oil is currently near $68-69 per barrel, essentially back to pre-war levels. The recovery in Hormuz flows has been the primary driver. The unresolved issue is Iran''''s stated intention to impose tanker tolls beginning in mid-August. This is currently not priced by the market but would create a floor on oil prices if it becomes a formal dispute in the next round.<br><br>
For your energy holdings, Canadian producers remain solidly profitable at current prices. The sector''''s dividend coverage and free cash flow profile are intact at $68-69 WTI. I will be in touch after the July 9 funeral completion with an update on whether the next negotiating round appears likely to resolve the toll question.<br><br>
[Your Name]<br><br>
<em>This communication is for educational purposes only and does not constitute personalized investment advice.</em>
</div>
