</div>',
  '<div class="toolkit-section">
<div class="toolkit-section-label">Client Profiles to Target</div>
<p><strong>DIY investors who bought energy stocks at the spring peak:</strong> Investors who chased TSX energy names in March-April near the $90-97 WTI peak are now sitting on unrealised losses with no framework for when to hold or exit. This is a high-probability prospecting window. They need a scenario framework, not a prediction.</p>
<p><strong>Investors who sold energy in June and are watching for re-entry:</strong> The Hormuz story created a clear sell signal for some investors around the MOU signing. Those who sold are now watching oil near pre-war levels and wondering whether the trade is over or whether the toll regime creates a second opportunity.</p>
<p><strong>Clients with Middle East travel or business exposure:</strong> Any client with professional or personal connections to the Gulf region is paying close attention to the Hormuz situation. The funeral pause and the toll regime tail risk are specific, current, and directly relevant to their interests.</p>
</div>
<div class="toolkit-section">
<div class="toolkit-section-label">Opening Line</div>
<div class="script-box">"I''''m calling because the Hormuz situation has reached a specific pivot point with the Doha talks and the Khamenei funeral, and there is one tail risk the market has not priced that I think is worth understanding before the next round of talks begins."</div>
</div>
<div class="toolkit-section">
<div class="toolkit-section-label">Value Proposition</div>
<p>The oil price story of 2026 has had three distinct phases: the war onset shock, the peak plateau, and the Hormuz normalisation decline. Most DIY investors experienced each phase reactively. The fourth phase, the mid-August toll deadline, is visible and upcoming. An advisor who identifies this inflection point before it becomes a headline event demonstrates exactly the forward-looking analytical value that distinguishes professional advice from news-driven self-direction.</p>
</div>
<div class="toolkit-section">
<div class="toolkit-section-label">Discovery Questions</div>
<p>How has the Hormuz situation affected your energy holdings this year, and what is your current exposure?</p>
<p>Did you make any changes to your portfolio after the June 17 MOU was announced?</p>
<p>Are you aware that Iran has stated an intention to impose tanker tolls beginning in mid-August, and do you have a view on how that affects Canadian energy?</p>
<p>Do you have an advisor who is tracking the specific negotiating milestones in the US-Iran talks for you?</p>
</div>
