Iran has stated in the Doha talks this week that it intends to impose tanker tolls on Hormuz transits beginning in mid-August, after the 60-day MOU negotiating window. The US categorically opposes this, characterising Hormuz as an international waterway with no legal basis for fees. If this disagreement is not resolved in the next round of talks, it would create a structural supply disruption distinct from the military escalation that drove the initial price spike.<br><br>
